#: ../../../platforms/creating_platform.rst:47
msgid "Packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/creating_platform.rst:49
msgid ""
"Some tools are the same when compiling for several platforms, for example a "
"common compiler. A *package* is some tool or framework that can be used when "
"compiling for one or multiple platforms. Even if multiple platforms use the "
"same package, the package only needs to be downloaded once. Since each "
"package is pre-built for the different host systems (Windows, Mac, Linux), "
"developers can get started without first compiling the tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../platforms/creating_platform.rst:57
msgid ""
"PlatformIO has a registry with pre-built packages for the most popular "
"operating systems and you can use them in your platform manifest. Custom "
"packages can be uploaded to the PlatformIO Registry using :ref:"
"`cmd_pkg_publish` command."
msgstr ""

